# Reverse-engineer Terraform from allocated state

Reference material. Stage notes own execution.

Keywords: import block, brownfield, codegen, aws.

## Goal

Turn each allocated state group into a readable Terraform root under
`aws/groups/<group_id>/` with versions, providers, imports, and generated
resource HCL. Prefer Terraform 1.5+ import blocks. Do not commit `*.tf.json`.

## Entry

Start from the run working directory artifacts (clone path, monolith state,
group manifests, group state paths). If count reconciliation failed, do not
scaffold HCL. Do not ask the operator for prior-phase artifacts.

## Success

Each group has importable HCL. Empty resource stubs are not enough. Addresses
that cannot be represented safely go to the orphans bundle with a short reason.

## Registry fit

When a group matches a known module, use a pinned source. Otherwise keep
explicit resource HCL.
